  "plan": {
    "goal": "Recapitulate mid-range venular wall shear (3 dyn/cm² = 0.3 Pa) on a HUVEC-lined microfluidic channel.",
    "rationale": "Venular endothelium experiences low-to-mid shear; 3 dyn/cm² (0.3 Pa) is a mid-range venular value within the HUVEC physiological shear window (0.1–1 Pa). A 400×100 µm channel at ~12 µL/min yields 0.3 Pa wall shear (Re 0.8, laminar; residence ~4 s over 20 mm; ΔP ~120 Pa, well within syringe-pump range). HUVEC seeded at 15,000 cells/cm² (midpoint of the 10,000–20,000 range) on the 0.08 cm² channel floor. Endothelial health is assessed by morphology and junctional markers (VE-cadherin), not TEER, since HUVEC barrier is low (~20–100 Ω·cm²).",
